heonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T23:43:42-08:00","id":392415,"title":"","content":"Let's talk about the cabal origins. How long have we been together? Do we have any unifying stuff besides being Mages? Do we have a cool name? My own thoughts:<br /> <br /> <br /> My first suggestion falls back on my history more, but it's the first one that comes to mind: I envision Astoria working to start the cabal in response to her mentor disappearing, originally under the auspice of trying to follow his trail. Not used to working alone (<i>frankly terrified of it</i>), she reached out for people to band together if just to stave off her own mental compulsions. Whether Phoenix/Bardo are people that she had conferred with before, or were simply in the right place at the right time, I leave to the both of you.<br /> <br /> (<i>I would like to note that Phoenix pointed out our cyclical &quot;Death-Prime-Life&quot; sympathetic connection in the other thread. Thematically, these are awesome.</i>)<br /> <br /> So, that said, any other ideas?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>edit:</b> I am going to switch out that dot of Hallow for Sanctum so that Bardo and I are enforcing a group space together. This could be a simple enough factor for them to have met; who can afford private space in Boston on their own these days?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4859,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","user":"NoiseConspiracy","date":". 02-04-2015, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T03:14:27-08:00","id":392483,"title":"","content":"First things first, here is Dr. Marvin's character sheet:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Player:</b> Thorbes<br /> <b>Chronicle:</b> Anthology of Power<br /> <br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Order:</b> Free Council<br /> <b>Cabal: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Prudence<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Pride<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Left-Handed Doctor<br /> <br /> <b><u>Advantages:</u></b><br /> Health: 7 (6 due to Pattern Scourging)<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Defense: 2<br /> Initiative: 7<br /> Speed: 9<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 2 (3 Merit dots invested to raise it from 1)<br /> Wisdom: 5 (Reduced due to the hubristic nature of his research. The extra 10xp are spent in 3 1-dot Merits and in buying the second dot of another)*<br /> Mana: 11 (2/turn)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u> </b><br /> Intelligence: 4<br /> Wits: 2<br /> Resolve: 2<br /> <br /> Strength: 1<br /> Dexterity: 3<br /> Stamina: 2 (1 due to Pattern Scourging)<br /> <br /> Presence: 2<br /> Manipulation: 2<br /> Composure: 4 (free dot from Path)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> Academics: 1<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation: 1<br /> Medicine: 4 (Surgery)<br /> Occult: 2 (the Soul)<br /> Politics: 1<br /> Science: 2 (Drugs)<br /> <br /> Athletics:<br /> Brawl:<br /> Drive: 1<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny: 1<br /> Stealth: 1<br /> Survival:<br /> Weaponry: 1<br /> <br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Empathy: 1<br /> Expression: 2<br /> Intimidation:<br /> Persuasion: 1<br /> Socialize: 1<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge: 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><br /> <br /> Resources: 3 (from his profitable job as a surgeon) [WoD: p.115]<br /> Status (Doctor): 2 (more or less informal status due to his skill)* [WoD: p.116]<br /> Library: 1 (the Soul)* [M:tA: p.85]<br /> Sanctum: 1 (small laboratory)* [M:tA: p.86]<br /> Hallow: 1 (inside the Sanctum, an small washing pile with a resonance of &quot;Cleansing&quot;)* [M.tA: p.83]<br /> High Speech: 1 (Free) [M:tA: p.84]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Arcana</u>:</b> Death 2, Life 2, Matter 2<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rotes</u></b><br /> Forensic Gaze (Death 1; M:tA: p.134)<br /> Soul Marks (Death 1; M:tA: p.135)<br /> Cleanse the Body (Life 1; M:tA: p.180)<br /> Pulse of the Living World (Life 1; M:tA: p.181)<br /> Transmute Water (Matter 2; M:tA: p.197)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> <br /> &quot;Aseptic&quot;: everything turns artificially quiet and clean and the smell of disinfectant permeates the ambience.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Biography</u></b><br /> <br /> Born the only son of a traditional bostonian couple that had suffered a couple of abortions, Marvin didn't seem long for this world. Sickly and weak since birth, the child managed to survive the first day of his life against all odds. Then he lived for a week. Then a month. Whether it was little Marvin's determination, the obsesive love of his parents, or something stranger still, the fact is that Marvin succeeded where his stillborn brothers couldn't and managed to grow up to became a child, then a teenager and finally a young adult that was the pride of his parents.<br /> <br /> Although his health was always precarious at best, or maybe as sort of strange compesation of nature, Marvin demonstrated from an early age a vivacious ingenuity and a sharp intellect. Good natured, he decided to use his prodigious faculties to help those like him and so, with the blessing of his parents, he studied to became a doctor. His analitical mind and strong memory served him well and he graduated as the first of his promotion.<br /> <br /> Now Marvin is growing old, his parents died not a couple of years ago and he visits their tomb and that of his stillborn brothers every week. Married to one of his younger colleages and co-workers at the hospital (working in the maternity wing) they still have no child of their own. On one hand the job consumes a lot of time from both of them, and Marvin secretely fears that he may be incapable of siring healthy children as happened to his parents. He doesn't want to visit more small tombs the weekends.<br /> <br /> The Awakening of Dr. Marvin Bates was at once more and less traumatic than most. He was beside the bed where their parents were dying of old age in his own hospital when, maybe due to the emotional overload, things started to get strange. He could felt how with each breath his parents were less and less alive, while nearby in the maternity ward the life was flourishing. As a certain undefinable spark was obviously getting extinguished in his parents, a new light grew stronger by the second in the newborns. Marvin finally awoke when he left the room where his parents laid dead to look for his wife to give her the news, only to saw the unmistakable gaze of his parents coming from a couple of recently born twins.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b><br /> <br /> Comfy appartement. Good german car. Extensive medical library.<br /> <br /> Path Tool: Scalpel.<br /> <br /> Death Tool: consecrated ashes from a cremated body.<br /> Life Tool: his own freshly spilt blood.<br /> Matter Tool(s): Salt, mercury and sulfur.<br /> <br /> <b>-Optional Details-</b><br /> <br /> <b>Age: </b>Early forties<br /> <b>Gender: </b>Male<br /> <b>Ethnicity: </b>American of british origin<br /> <b>Nationality: </b>American<br /> <b>Hair Color: </b>Salt and pepper with still mostly black hair, very open forehead. Invariably clean shaven.<br /> <b>Eye Color: </b>Blue-gray<br /> <b>Sexuality:</b> Heterosexual<br /> <b>Spirituality:</b> Marvin believes in reincarnation, specifically in the greek concept of Metempsycosis (also known as Transmigration). He thinks it is his duty to discover the proccess now that he's been given the tools to do so.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Health : </b>[][][][][][]<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 4/6<br /> <b>Mana:</b> 7/11</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Experience Log:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Experience Total:</b> 13<br /> <b>Experience Current:</b> 3<br /> <b>Experience spent:</b><br /> <i>1st dot Hallow Merit</i> (2xp)<br /> <i>1st dot Sanctum Merit</i> (2xp)<br /> <i>1st dot Library Merit</i> (2xp)<br /> <i>2nd dot Stauts Merit</i> (4xp)<br /> <b>Total Spent:</b> 10xp</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now, as per the biography he's been barely a couple of years Awake so I supose that's the longer we could have been a Cabal. Otherwise I can change it so he's been awakened longer, it is not specially relevant for the concept, though probably no more than 5-7 years?<br /> <br /> I chose Free Council a bit by default, but I think he could make a good Mysterium too, that way we could have met in the Atheneaum or something. Maybe through casual conversation about the nature of your role as a an artifact hunter you mentioned something about one that may pertain to Bardo's interests and so decided to keep you close. I supose you could have &quot;recruited&quot; Phoenix at some point as bodyguard and the two of you were already a proto-cabal when we met.<br /> <br /> The Prime-Life-Death suggest a cicle of creation(Prime), death(duh) and rebirth (Life). Maybe we could call our Cabal &quot;The Ouroboros&quot;?<br /> <br /> If we pool the Sanctum Merit, as you suggested, we can have a living room next to the laboratory/ritual room to hang around.<br /> <br /> EDIT: regarding the cabal name,it seems in Boston theres already a lot of ouroboros imagery, its some cabal's symbol (the Special Media Group) and it is on the presentation card of another (the Gravediggers).<br /> <br /> Another Prime-Life-Death symbol could be a phoenix, but it is also the Shadow Name of one of the Cabal members wich could lead to confussion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-28-2015, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T11:23:25-08:00","id":392757,"title":"","content":"Right now just waiting on Crapcarp to post his Template and to give his opinion on the Cabal. After that, everyone can roll Initiative and we'll be good to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T13:01:59-08:00","id":392912,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Character Sheet</u></b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Player:</u> Epicarp (or crapcarp, whichever you prefer)<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Anthology of Power<br /> <br /> <u>Shadow Name:</u> Phoenix<br /> <u>Sleeper Name:</u> Garrick Royce (this is not his real name, that's below. Rather, this is the name he uses when among Sleepers or other supernaturals)<br /> <u>Real Name:</u> Kemp Walt Dexter<br /> <br /> <u>Path:</u> Obrimos<br /> <u>Order:</u> Adamantine Arrow<br /> <u>Cabal:</u><br /> <u>Legacy:</u> (Tamer of Fire; Legacies: the Ancient p. 39)<br /> <br /> <u>Virtue:</u> Faith<br /> <u>Vice:</u> Wrath<br /> <u>Concept:</u> Hero in a World of Darkness<br /> <br /> <b><u>Advantages:</u></b><br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Defense: 2<br /> Initiative: 4<br /> Speed: 11<br /> Size: 5<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 3<br /> Wisdom: 5<br /> Mana: 5/12<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u> </b><br /> Intelligence: 2<br /> Wits: 3<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> <br /> Strength: 4<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Presence: 3<br /> Manipulation: 1<br /> Composure: 2<br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> Academics:<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Medicine: 2<br /> Occult: 2 (Mythology)<br /> Politics:<br /> Science:<br /> <br /> Athletics: 3<br /> Brawl: 4 (Muay Thai)<br /> Drive:<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Stealth:<br /> Survival:<br /> Weaponry: 4 (Polearms)<br /> <br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Empathy: 2<br /> Expression: 3<br /> Intimidation: 2<br /> Persuasion:<br /> Socialize:<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><ul><li>Muay Thai - Aggressive Striking (2; WoD p. 110, Armory Reloaded p. 65 &amp; 110)</li> <li>Staff Fighting (1; Armory p. 213)</li> <li>Status - Adamantine Arrow (1; MtAw p. 88)</li> <li>High Speech (1; Core p. 84)</li> <li>Status - Dojo (1; WoD p. 116)<br /> <br /> He works at a local dojo that has some good weapons. Among other things, this allows him to borrow some of these weapons so long as he can justify it in some way. I'll let the ST decide on the specifics of the weapons and what's needed to convince his employer to borrow them.</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Arcana</u>:</b> Forces 2, Mind 2, Prime 1, Life 1<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rotes</u></b><ul><li>Kinetic Blow (Forces; 2; Strength + Brawl or Weaponry + Forces; Core p. 166)</li> <li>Sense Consciousness (Mind; 1; Wits + Empathy + Mind; Core p. 206)</li> <li>Mental Shield (Mind; 2; Resolve + Occult + Mind; Core p. 208)</li> <li>Cleanse the Body (Life; 1; Stamina + Medicine + Life; Core p.180)</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Weak or Uncloaked to Sleepers</i> - There's a hint of invigoration in the immediate surroundings. Colors are a bit more vibrant, light shines a bit brighter, blood pumps a bit quicker.<br /> <br /> <i>Strong or Uncloaked to Mages</i> - The hint becomes a full-on rush, everything seems to take on a life of its own as their Fallen skin begins to crack. In the distance, a voice can be heard.<br /> <br /> <i>Powerful</i> - The cracks widen with thin beams of Supernal light breaking through. The distant voice becomes a choir singing High Speech, as if complimenting an epic scene.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Biography</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Asleep</i> - He was always that problem kid at school, the one you'd swore would end up in jail after graduation (assuming he would graduate, that is). Whether it was beating up kids or sticking it to the Man (be them teachers or otherwise), it seemed he spent more time in the office than in the classroom. It wasn't that he had a problem with authority, he always showed respect and discipline to his martial arts trainer, he just had a problem with bullshit.<br /> <br /> Even as a Sleeper, he could always see past a bit of the Lie. Probably because he enjoyed mythology so much. The tall tales and epic exploits spoke to him in ways people either didn't know how, didn't want to, or perhaps were afraid to. It was fiction on the surface, but truth rang underneath, so long as one was willing to listen. And that frustrated him to no end...<br /> <br /> <i>Awakened</i> - Shortly after Awakening he moved to Boston and joined the Adamantine Arrow there. Since then, he's rapidly progressed in magic, if a little too much (the Awakened world has its fair share of bullshit, and since he tends to get violent in response, well...). Every night, he dreams of a certain Rune. What this Rune is and what it means is a one of the many Mysteries he'll have to chase.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b><ul><li>Order Tool - Bo Staff (Damage 2B; Size 4N; Durability 1; +1 Defense in melee combat; Armory p. 32)</li> <li>Forces Tool - Magnetic Gloves (<a href=\"http://toolmonger.com/2007/12/13/hot-or-not-silverback-magnetic-glove/\" target=\"_blank\">http://toolmonger.com/2007/12/13/hot...agnetic-glove/</a>)</li> <li>Sports Car (Durability 2; Size 10; Structure 12; Acceleration 15; Safe Speed 103 [70 mph], Maximum Speed 235 [160 mph], Handling 4)</li> </ul><br /> <b><u>Experience</u></b><br /> Unspent: 3<br /> Spent: 10<br /> <br /> <b>-Optional Details-</b><br /> <u>Age:</u> 19<br /> <u>Gender:</u> Male<br /> <u>Ethnicity:</u> Probably mixed, given his tan skin tone<br /> <u>Nationality:</u> American<br /> <u>Hair Color:</u> Grey<br /> <u>Eye Color:</u> Brown<br /> <u>Sexuality:</u> None of my business<br /> <u>Spirituality:</u> The Monomyth if that counts<br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> Get up, morning ritual, go to school, try to learn as best you can, beat up those same assholes again, blah blah blah. Rinse and repeat. Every. Single. Damn. Day. And after 12 years of this drivel? Just work from here on out now. It's the same dance, just a slightly different tune.<br /> <br /> It felt like Death. He always hated Death, hates it even now. Since when was stagnation ever necessary in the universe anyways?<br /> <br /> He couldn't just fade away on some deathbed. There had to be more to life than this. They may have been fairy tales, but there was truth to the various myths he enjoyed. The heroic journey, it was real, it had to be! The devil was in finding it. That's when she showed up.<br /> <br /> &quot;In order to escape, you have to risk everything,&quot; she said. While she looked somewhere in her thirties, it seemed as though she contained the wisdom of sages beyond the years of mortals.<br /> <br /> He immediately understood what that meant, he knew what needed to be done, but he just didn't know how to go about it. It was like a riddle he knew the answer to, but couldn't find the words to explain it. He racked his brain, trying to figure it out. And he had to do it quick because it was only a few days until graduation, a few days of freedom. Once those passed, he'd be stuffed right back in the machine and that woman would leave. He didn't know how he knew, but he knew.<br /> <br /> In order to escape, you have to risk everything.<br /> <br /> &quot;But how do I risk everything? Where do I go? Where do I look?&quot; he asked her, giving in. He didn't want to resort to calling for help. It was one of those things where you had to figure it out yourself, wasn't it? Asking was cheating, right? But he had no choice, he was simply out of time.<br /> <br /> She let out a slight chuckle. &quot;I was wondering when you were going to ask that.&quot;<br /> <br /> The walls flew away in fright, revealing a landscape of dreams and stars. Truth rang like bells, wisdom performing a harmony unmatched by any human composer. The birthplace of myth. High atop a distant Watchtower shone the light of a golden key. That was the Call, now to answer it.<br /> <br /> Archetypes sprang forth to challenge him. They were the Trials. He defeated them, every victory pouring enlightenment beyond his wildest dreams into him, making every trial easier than the last. He was on a roll, he was going to reach that Watchtower in no time. This is what he wanted after all. And now that he has the opportunity, he wasn't going to let it go.<br /> <br /> Overcoming the last trial, he entered the Watchtower with gleeful anticipation. His expectation of wondrous grandeur was met with painful reality. He wished for a way out of the machine, and a way out this Watchtower would give. But the world he would enter was filled with shadows and secrets, terrible truths and dark paths. And he could never go back once he entered. The Cave.<br /> <br /> His horrifying realization twisted itself into a dragon, and he ran. Ran away to whence he came, trying to escape the corrupting breaths behind him. It wasn't worth it. Nothing was worth this world of darkness. The machine may be boring, but at least one could be sane in there. This new world threatened insanity as the least of its punishments. Only a madman would ever choose to go there.<br /> <br /> He saw the machine in sight, and that's when he stopped. Why? Why wouldn't his legs move? It was only a few steps now, he was right there. He couldn't afford to be in this other world. The dragon approached, each step shaking the ground. Just a few more steps, but something in him just wouldn't budge. The dragon was right behind him, inhaling a lungful.<br /> <br /> In order to escape, you have to risk everything.<br /> <br /> The fire of his soul lit, and he let out a defiant roar against the dragon's breath. This world he knows may be filled with darkness, but that doesn't mean he has to take it lying down. In fact, he owed the world not to take it lying down. It was his duty to conquer this darkness like he did with the dragon, to shine as a hero. Dragons may exist, but they can be killed. He carved his name into the dragon, marking his first victory. Everything faded back into mundane reality, the woman wearing a smirk.<br /> <br /> &quot;That was the Threshold Guardian,&quot; she explained, &quot;For the rest, you're going to have to come with me.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Status</u></b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Health: 0000000<br /> Willpower: 4/5<br /> Mana: 5/12<br /> Wisdom: 5</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u><b>XP Log</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Experience (Unspent/Total): 3/13<br /> <br /> Dots Purchased - XP Cost/Total XP Spent<br /> Muay Thai 2 - 4/4<br /> Staff Fighting 1 - 2/6<br /> Status (AA) 1 - 2/8<br /> High Speech 1 - 0/8<br /> Status (Dojo) 1 - 2/10</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As far as the peeps meeting up, both NC and Thorbes's ideas are pretty good. Perhaps Astoria met Phoenix in a library several times before Fell's disappearance, as Phoenix likes to read mythology (that, and the fact that it's warmer than his dinky little apartment as he <i>hates</i> the cold) and Astoria might go there for artifact research and/or personal interests as well. I would also point out a little thing in Astoria's backstory saying she learned some self-defense, but the only combat-related Skill she has is Firearms, which she would never learn from Phoenix, not just because he has no dots in it, but also the fact that he literally detests guns (he sees them as the cheapshot of weaponry), so I highly doubt she would meet Phoenix that way.<br /> <br /> As for the cabal's name and theme, there's a great Rule of Three thing going on with both the cabal already and the chronicle itself, so I think it'd be best to focus on that. I just don't know what to use exactly. There's so many things related to 3 that I can't choose, any ideas from you guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 02-27-2015, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T13:12:38-08:00","id":392942,"title":"","content":"Completely understood.<br /> <br /> Sanctum: I'm okay with something like this, whether it was just a living space. On a long enough timeline, Astoria would probably want to start building a library, so that would be it's eventual purpose. Since I'm essentially building whatever I work with off of your space, I'll leave it up to you to describe first.<br /> <br /> Cabal: I really like the idea of us having a group name, but I think it's because the sort of thing Astoria would be really into; giving something a name gives it purpose, and that's why she was seeking others out. I was trying to think of other cyclical-types of things that would be fit for creation or fortune, and I kept coming back to the word &quot;Halo.&quot; I think it can mean a similar thing, paired with something appropriate. Spitballing a few ideas here:<br /> <br /> <i>Order of the Halo</i> - If we're more monk-like.<br /> <i>The Halo Group</i> - If we're more professional.<br /> <br /> I have an urge to suggest <i>The Candlestick Opera</i>, but that sounds like total cheese when I say it out loud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T13:25:17-08:00","id":392951,"title":"","content":"Nice catch on the 3's Crapcarp! Three Mages in the Protagonist Cabal. Three Mages in the Prologue.<br /> <br /> It might interest you to note that the dates and times, from the Prologue and the initial IC post, Numerologically equal 3.<br /> <br /> April 13 1984: 4+1+1+9+8+7=30, 3+0=3<br /> January 3rd 2017 8:24pm: 3+3+2+0+1+7+8+2+4=30, 3+0=3<br /> <br /> I thought it was great when you guys came up with the Prime, Death, Life=Birth, Death, Reincarnation thing, thus continuing this Rule of Three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T13:34:11-08:00","id":392966,"title":"","content":"Alright, you guys don't have to wait to sort out the Cabal name and such before getting started. Unless you just prefer it that way. You could leave the Cabal details in the background, or if you decide that the Cabal has just gotten together your characters could be working on these things right along with the Players.<br /> <br /> If you guys want to go ahead, feel free to roll Initiative. This will set our posting order until the next Chapter. Whoever has the high Initiative can post, if you guys decide to go ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T13:55:46-08:00","id":393002,"title":"","content":"Well, it looks like I rolled a 3, so that gives me a grand total of 6. Good luck to the rest of you all.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I like the feel of rolling dice, but you're sure of us rolling here instead of using a communal roller? Not that I'm insinuating or complaining, it's just what I'm used to...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T14:03:56-08:00","id":393012,"title":"","content":"We can go with a dice roller if the Honor System makes people uncomfortable. One of the reasons I wanted to be selective about character creation is because I felt it would up the odds of finding mature players, ones who would be honest about their rolls.<br /> <br /> How do the rest of you feel about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T20:23:09-08:00","id":393353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NoiseConspiracy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=393002#post393002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it looks like I rolled a 3, so that gives me a grand total of 6. Good luck to the rest of you all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, if you rolled a 3, wouldn't the total be 9 instead of 6?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=392966#post392966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, you guys don't have to wait to sort out the Cabal name and such before getting started. Unless you just prefer it that way. You could leave the Cabal details in the background, or if you decide that the Cabal has just gotten together your characters could be working on these things right along with the Players.<br /> <br /> If you guys want to go ahead, feel free to roll Initiative. This will set our posting order until the next Chapter. Whoever has the high Initiative can post, if you guys decide to go ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good! I rolled a 1, so that's a 5 for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=393012#post393012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can go with a dice roller if the Honor System makes people uncomfortable. One of the reasons I wanted to be selective about character creation is because I felt it would up the odds of finding mature players, ones who would be honest about their rolls.<br /> <br /> How do the rest of you feel about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, frankly if I wanted to cheat with an online dice roller I could and none of you would ever know, so to me it doesn't matter whether we use this Honor System or not. I'll play honestly either way because life would never be fun if you always won.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T03:07:43-08:00","id":393580,"title":"","content":"<b>Initiative:</b> 7 + <i>8</i> = <b>15</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ooops, seems I'm going first... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Such responsability!<br /> <br /> I trust in the honor and integrity of my fellow players and Storyteller, and hope I get trusted in return <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Even in free-form roleplay I get my character to fail a lot, sometimes spectacularly because is more fun this way. And finally will be using my Mage dice in an actual Mage game! How can I let that opportunity pass by? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @NoiseConspiracy: We have Library in the making, it is only about matters of the soul for now, but the more dots we pool, the best it will get.<br /> <br /> As for the Cabal Name: why not directly call us &quot;The Rule of 3&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Holly Ominous Title Image, Batman!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-05-2015, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T07:18:28-08:00","id":393726,"title":"","content":"Looks like we're sticking with the Honor System. I hope you feel comfortable with that NoiseConspiracy. I'm personally glad, as its the way I had intended it and, like I said, I love the feel of dice in my hand<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:17:56-08:00","id":393922,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with it. I've just played in a lot of games with militant players that didn't like the perceived nature of what is and what isn't &quot;fair.&quot; I don't have an issue, I'm just not used to it...that's all.<br /> <br /> The Rule of Three works for now. Maybe there is an in-character discussion about whether it can be changed.<br /> <br /> So the base premise is that Astoria's mentor left, and she seeks out to build her own cabal. She &quot;hires&quot; Phoenix as protection, and teams up with Barto due to the lack of sanctum space in Boston (as well as their mutual interests). Make no mistake, she is not a &quot;leader&quot; of the group, but potentially seeks out the cabal to work together than the others do perhaps? As per usual, correct me if I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> (Crapcarp, it would be a 9, you're right. I forgot it's adding both scores and not the higher of the two)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:38:45-08:00","id":393936,"title":"","content":"I like to think I'm pretty good at weeding out problem players. Its often easy to spot during character creation if you pay attention. One of the things I look for is whether or not players make a fuss when I ask them to change things on their character sheet. It gives me a good snapshot of what their priorities are, and how well they work with a group. In return I work with my Players and do everything I can to ensure they get to have the character they want, and that we all enjoy the game. I think this group is going to work well together<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T14:26:53-08:00","id":394112,"title":"","content":"I hope my change of allocations didn't let me in a bad place, then.<br /> <br /> Ok, so as it seems I'm going first....<br /> <br /> Should I get right to those thre hours before the meeting, or may I perhaps show some little snapshots of what constitutes the everyday life of Dr. Bates? You know, his morning rituals, a bit of the relationship with his wife, a bit of work, research as mage, etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T19:06:31-08:00","id":394358,"title":"","content":"By all means Thorbes. Add as much detail as you like. The more the better as far as I'm concerned. Oh, and just the opposite. You were perfectly willing to work with me when I asked you to change your Attributes, showing you were a mature player. I appreciated it.<br /> <br /> Also, a Cabal name submitted for your consideration: The Trinity Cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-05-2015, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T05:59:12-08:00","id":394711,"title":"","content":"Sounds nice! I'll just refer to the ritual place as Cabal's Sanctum until everybody agrees on the name.<br /> <br /> Ok, minor OOC skill rolls here, more as a test than anything:<br /> <br /> <b>Rutinary Heart Surgery:</b> Dexterity (3) + Medicine (4) + Specialty (Surgery)= 1,4,7,7,<b>8</b>,<b>8</b>,<b>9</b>,<b>10</b> (Re-roll=3) = <b>4 Successes</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul Marks Rote:</b> Intelligence (4) + Medicine (4) + Death (2)= 3,4,4,7,<b>8</b>,<b>8</b>,<b>8</b>,<b>8</b>,<b>10</b>,<b>10</b> (Re-roll=3,3) = <b>6 Successes</b>.<br /> <br /> Also, sorry for the awfully long post. Next ones would be shorter, but I needed to present the character in his three facets as Husband (Marvin), Surgeon (Dr.Bates) and Mage (Bardo). I though I should add my personal note to the underlaying rule of three theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T07:20:51-08:00","id":394787,"title":"","content":"Great post to get us started Thorbes. I love what you're doing with the threes, and the added details about your character's life really brings the story alive, and gives me stuff to work with later on<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T09:40:00-08:00","id":395006,"title":"","content":"My into is not quite as dense as Bardo's, but I figured it's just about easing in for the moment before we do to the meat and potatoes of the meal. Astoria refers to their Sanctum as &quot;The Nest,&quot; although this doesn't have to be a shared term...she had a tendency to give nicknames to most things that don't have one.<br /> <br /> Side note: these forums aren't exactly mobile-friendly, are they? That's the last time I write a big post and try to put it up while at work via phone.<br /> <br /> (Apologies to any typos or autocorrects that I may have not caught yet.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T14:05:01-08:00","id":395367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=394711#post394711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, sorry for the awfully long post. Next ones would be shorter, but I needed to present the character in his three facets as Husband (Marvin), Surgeon (Dr.Bates) and Mage (Bardo). I though I should add my personal note to the underlaying rule of three theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel ya man, my intro was pretty long as well. You just don't think about it when you're writing until you stop and see for yourself, and by then you don't wanna delete all the stuff you wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T14:25:10-08:00","id":395381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=395367#post395367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel ya man, my intro was pretty long as well. You just don't think about it when you're writing until you stop and see for yourself, and by then you don't wanna delete all the stuff you wrote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear, hear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My internet went down mid-writing so I copy-pasted it to word and continue writing, then I saw I was about to hit the third page and just stoped for sanity's sake <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T14:30:42-08:00","id":395405,"title":"","content":"So now that we all posted, is my turn again, or should the Storyteller set the scene?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T14:35:31-08:00","id":395454,"title":"","content":"You know you've got a great group of players when they're complaining that their posts are too <b>long</b>.<br /> <br /> This was a great series of opening posts guys, I'm very happy with this group! My role doesn't kick back in until you guys go to see Meristoktrix, so lets have another round of posts where you guys interact at the Nest. You guys should feel free to interact there as much as you like. It gives me a wonderful array of stuff to use later on. As soon as you guys head to the Tap Room, I'll make my next post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T15:00:00-08:00","id":395481,"title":"","content":"Ok, guys, so should we skip to when you start to arrive to The Nest, first Astoria, then Phoenix? Bardo's been there for almost all the afternoon. Maybe I can perform some protection rituals (Prudence, you now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) while you get there, it would take a good 3 hours at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T15:10:44-08:00","id":395491,"title":"","content":"Yes, for the sake of flow I think it best to have them both arrive during your post Thorbes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T15:33:43-08:00","id":395510,"title":"","content":"Ok, it's settled then. Don't expect a block of text as the first one tough<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <b>Body Control Spell:</b> Gnosis (2) + Life (2) + High Speech (2) + Willpower (3) - 4 (Duration: 12 hours) = 2,4,6,<b>10</b>,<b>10</b> (Re-roll=<b>8</b>,<b>9</b>) = <b>4 Successes (Potency)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effects:</b> for 12 hours Bardo will enjoy the following benefits:<br /> <br /> <i>Needs eight times as less oxigen as usual<br /> +4 Initiative (for a total of 19)<br /> Can go for eight times as much time without food/rest before deprivation/fatigue settles in.<br /> Poisons/toxins take 8 times the normal period between damage effects.<br /> Heals a level of Bashing Damage every 30 seconds.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <br /> <b>Current Mana:</b> 4<br /> <br /> <b>Current Willpower:</b> 5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  added final Initiative value after bonuses. 02-06-2015, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T17:14:58-08:00","id":395650,"title":"","content":"Can I just say....I love this magic system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T09:30:41-08:00","id":396418,"title":"","content":"For some reason, my message alert didn't trigger this last conversation about getting that ball rolling back out of the Nest, so my post was more about settling in. <br /> <br /> Phoenix, you want to write yourself into the room and then back out with us to the meeting, or should I revise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T09:47:34-08:00","id":396429,"title":"","content":"Spend all the time you like having your characters interact at the Nest. What I said to Thorbes was simply to make sure your characters arrive during his post, which he did.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Arrive at the Nest that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-07-2015, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T03:11:17-08:00","id":397327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NoiseConspiracy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=396418#post396418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, my message alert didn't trigger this last conversation about getting that ball rolling back out of the Nest, so my post was more about settling in.<br /> <br /> Phoenix, you want to write yourself into the room and then back out with us to the meeting, or should I revise?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you have to revise if you don't want to. I can work with it well enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> [Imp cast Supernal Vision (M:tA p. 221): Gnosis + Prime = 4 dice; 4 successes to Potency (9,9,4,<b>10</b>,<b>10</b>,7)]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 02-08-2015, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T04:42:41-08:00","id":397358,"title":"","content":"I think short posts are better when some dialogue is to be had between characters. What do you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T05:57:14-08:00","id":397430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=397358#post397358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think short posts are better when some dialogue is to be had between characters. What do you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Certainly when it comes to basic &quot;hey how are you&quot; dialogue. I figure a good general rule is to have one sizable post at the beginning of every chapter, and any others beyond that will just depend on the situation, and what your character has to contribute to the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T12:53:29-08:00","id":397922,"title":"","content":"Crapcarp, those artifacts are just sort of color for the scene. Sort of showing her occupation at the forefront, but do nothing of real consequence. It may be up to Techpriest if they have any interesting effects to go with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T02:48:37-08:00","id":398628,"title":"","content":"Damm, I was re-reading the rules or Oblations to confirm they took an hour (we haven't that much time left) and reading about Hallows I had completely forgot they gave you a 1 point Mana discount in their vincinity. Bardo shouldn't have lost that Mana due to that Improvised Life spell (the Hallow is in the laboratory) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T03:50:14-08:00","id":398642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NoiseConspiracy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=397922#post397922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crapcarp, those artifacts are just sort of color for the scene. Sort of showing her occupation at the forefront, but do nothing of real consequence. It may be up to Techpriest if they have any interesting effects to go with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I thought they had some significance. Ah well, it's not like I didn't spend any Mana or anything, no harm done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T06:09:13-08:00","id":398730,"title":"","content":"Alright guys, moving on for flow, this next set of posts should take us to the meeting at the Lower Depths Tap Room. Please describe any preparations, how you get there (on foot, by car, train, etc), if you guys take your weapons, and where you keep them (Would Phoenix walk around the city with his staff? Does Astoria have a shoulder rig for her gun? Would either of them bring a weapon into the bar, or leave it in a vehicle? Etc.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Crapcarp, I'm curious why you didn't bring up the Rune?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-09-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:48:49-08:00","id":399198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=398730#post398730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crapcarp, I'm curious why you didn't bring up the Rune?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I forgot. This is what happens when I write posts late at night and wanna rush to bed. I'll fix it up, though. I don't think it'll take much to incorporate the character's reactions in the same posts for going to the meeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:04:37-08:00","id":399205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=399198#post399198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, I forgot. This is what happens when I write posts late at night and wanna rush to bed. I'll fix it up, though. I don't think it'll take much to incorporate the character's reactions in the same posts for going to the meeting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no worries man, I was just curious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:13:51-08:00","id":399402,"title":"","content":"Well, I had set the scene as just before leaving. NoiseConspiracy can maybe take care of the travel itself and crapcarp the arriving? Then it would be your turn again to set the new scene, right, Techpriest? Or maybe we can arrive in NoiseConspiracie's post and crapcarp gets the first post after the new scene is set by Techpriest? I didn't feel confident about narrating the travel, I have too many holes in my knowledge of transportation in Boston.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T19:58:36-08:00","id":399852,"title":"","content":"You guys don't have to be specific about roads or anything. After all, we never really said where The Nest even is. Given that this is the middle of a major blizzard your options are pretty much walking, or walking and train. (Do blizzards shut down trains? I wouldn't know, I live a warm area without trains. I think Boston's rails are mostly above ground.)<br /> <br /> So it looks like the guys will follow whatever Astoria does. I'm more interested in what, if any, gear you guys have with you than the travel details. Any discrepancies with reality can always fall under &quot;the World of Darkness is different from our own&quot; (Although The Lower Depths Tap Room is actually a real place). After NC and Carp have posted, I'll set the next scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-09-2015, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T08:21:08-08:00","id":400330,"title":"","content":"I've just realised Bardo didn't answer Astoria's question, how impolite! I'll edit a line in.<br /> <br /> EDIT: done <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-10-2015, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link