"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T17:21:35-08:00","id":405332,"title":"","content":"I went ahead and rolled all your Perception (Wits + Composure) dice. I felt it was an appropriate type of roll, given that if you all failed you wouldn't know anything was happening, in addition to preventing the need for another cycle. Let me know if you guys prefer a more meticulous, roll by roll type of game. I'm really good either way, personally. In fact if you guys prefer you can go ahead and roll Perception and I'll edit my post accordingly.<br /> <br /> Astoria: 1 Success<br /> Phoneix: 3 Successes<br /> Bardo: 0 Successes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T21:51:12-08:00","id":405458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=405332#post405332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went ahead and rolled all your Perception (Wits + Composure) dice. I felt it was an appropriate type of roll, given that if you all failed you wouldn't know anything was happening, in addition to preventing the need for another cycle. Let me know if you guys prefer a more meticulous, roll by roll type of game. I'm really good either way, personally. In fact if you guys prefer you can go ahead and roll Perception and I'll edit my post accordingly.<br /> <br /> Astoria: 1 Success<br /> Phoneix: 3 Successes<br /> Bardo: 0 Successes</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can stick with the rolls (of course <i>I</i> can <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) but I'm willing to make my own roll if everyone else wants to. Speaking of rolls...<br /> <br /> [Imp cast Supernal Vision w/ conjunctional Mind (M:tAw p.221): Gnosis + Prime = 4 dice; 1 success]<br /> <br /> And with Mage Sight on, he's gonna be looking around for resonance or anything else outta the ordinary. Not sure what to roll, though. I mean, I was thinking just the usual Intelligence + Occult, but he's not scrutinizing anything specific, just trying to see what's there, at least for now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T04:42:06-08:00","id":405698,"title":"","content":"Wow, Bardo is completely spaced out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hope Phoenix can blast that <i>evil painting thing</i> before it stabs us on the back or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T06:06:01-08:00","id":405741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=405332#post405332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went ahead and rolled all your Perception (Wits + Composure) dice. I felt it was an appropriate type of roll, given that if you all failed you wouldn't know anything was happening, in addition to preventing the need for another cycle. Let me know if you guys prefer a more meticulous, roll by roll type of game. I'm really good either way, personally. In fact if you guys prefer you can go ahead and roll Perception and I'll edit my post accordingly.<br /> <br /> Astoria: 1 Success<br /> Phoneix: 3 Successes<br /> Bardo: 0 Successes</div> </div> </div> </div>I am alright with this when it is in the interest of keeping things moving. The game essentially slows down by a day or two if we have to cycle through perception checks.<br /> <br /> We're this something more detrimental, like casting or such, I would balk at it. This is good for me.<br /> <br /> Edit: since we saw the painting, can I make any rolls to see what I can see with it? Or do I need to wait for Phoenix and Bardo to go before I can roll for Supernal Vision as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4859,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","user":"NoiseConspiracy","date":".  More words 02-14-2015, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T06:22:48-08:00","id":405743,"title":"","content":"Go ahead and roll NC. Once you have, I'll let you guys know what you see, then Carp can post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T07:26:01-08:00","id":405769,"title":"","content":"<i>Supernal Vision: Eye of the Magus (rote pg. 221) Wits 3 + Occult 2 + Prime 1 = 6, 4, 6, 4, <b>9</b>, 6 = 1 success.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T13:12:15-08:00","id":406065,"title":"","content":"Alright, well I'mma gonna go on ahead and make that scrutiny roll on the resonance of that painting demon/spirit/whatever the hell it is.<br /> <br /> [Scrutinizing resonance: Intelligence + Occult + 1 = 5 dice; 2 successes]<br /> <br /> I gave a +1 because based on the description, it looks to be a refined aura. The last die was a 6, so if you want me to take away the modifier, the roll would still be 2 successes (of course, I have no problem with rerolling if you prefer). I'll put one success in identity (he most likely won't recognize it, but if it ever shows up again he will) and one in nature. Yeah, it certainly isn't human, but I'm gonna put further successes into the nature to see exactly what it is.<br /> <br /> Do I have to roll Stamina to overcome the nausea as well, or has that just passed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T15:12:16-08:00","id":406135,"title":"","content":"Nah, the nausea was simply part of the Mage Sight. It passes quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T05:42:22-08:00","id":406604,"title":"","content":"Are we still in initiative? Or should crapcarp and I be posting since we had the vision?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T06:16:25-08:00","id":406612,"title":"","content":"EDIT: ok, maybe I should wait and see what Techpriest answers to NC.<br /> <br /> As Bardo seems completely oblivious to the paiting thing I supose he cannot try to scrutinize it himself. On the other hand people around him are flashing Mage Sight like it was getting out of style, so maybe he can be clued in?<br /> <br /> What he probably notice are the three new customers at the bar, if nothing else because there are so little people and with the waitress greeting them he should be aware of them.<br /> <br /> I'll try to direct Meristrokix attention to those three people, trying to ask without actually speaking if they may be some of the sleepers than had been following him. Should I roll something to do so?<br /> <br /> Bardo will also cast an Improvised Matter Knowing spell to see if they have weapons on them.<br /> <br /> <b>Matter Spell:</b> High Speech (2) + Gnosis (2) + Matter (2) - 4 (3 Targets) = 7, <b>9</b> = <b>1 Success</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:44:29-08:00","id":406827,"title":"","content":"Yes, we're still in initiative. It's Throbes' post now. In general I'll respond to Players questions so that the next Player will have those answers to work from, and the Players will continue on in Initiative. However, if you guys agree among yourselves to break Initiative for any particular reason, that's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T13:06:24-08:00","id":406934,"title":"","content":"If it's alright, Phoenix will scrutinize the auras of the newcomers.<br /> <br /> [Scrutinizing auras: Intelligence + Occult = 4 dice; 2 successes]<br /> <br /> Put both in nature, Phoenix wants to see whether these guys are actually Sleepers, or perhaps mages disguising themselves as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T13:46:56-08:00","id":406955,"title":"","content":"Thorbes: It seemed reasonable to me that if Matter 1 allows you to detect particular substances, and Forces 1 allows you to see heat, thus allowing you to see individuals through walls and such, that a Matter 2 Knowing spell would allow you to search for particular types of objects. (Hopefully this doesn't come back to bite me in the ass later)<br /> <br /> Phoenix: They still appear to be Sleepers.<br /> <br /> This brings up an interesting point though. Scrutiny can be performed as an Extended Action, with each roll representing a turn. In the interest of efficiency, any time you guys want to perform an Extended Action, you can go ahead and make several rolls (to a maximum number equaling your dice pool, as per the rules for Extended Actions), and list your successes. I will then describe the results as they come up. If your character is forced to do something that brakes his concentration on the Extended Action, he can put it on hold, or abandon it altogether, and the extra rolls simply won't occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T14:32:34-08:00","id":406991,"title":"","content":"Ok, Armor up, just in case:<br /> <br /> <b>Matter Mage Armor:</b> High Speech (2) + Gnosis (2) + Matter (2) = 6,6,7,<b>8</b>,<b>8</b>,<b>10</b> (Re-roll= 4) = <b>3 Successes (Potency)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> 2 points of Armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  added effect for clarity after NC. 02-16-2015, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T15:17:18-08:00","id":407039,"title":"","content":"Alright, normally the post order would pass to me, but since I've given ample info for Astoria to react too already, we'll move on to NC's post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T21:26:35-08:00","id":407376,"title":"","content":"Fate 2: Fortune's Protection (pg. 152) <i>High Speech 2 + Gnosis 1 + Fate 2 = 9, 6, 2, 8, 9 = 3 successes.<br /> <br /> +2 armor for duration of scene.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T03:14:26-08:00","id":407543,"title":"","content":"Guess Phoenix'll follow suit with his own armor.<br /> <br /> [Imp cast Unseen Shield (M:tAw p.167): Gnosis + Forces = 5 dice; 4 successes]<br /> <br /> I'm gonna go on ahead with my post, editing it afterwards if necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T07:53:52-08:00","id":407730,"title":"","content":"We'll skip Thorbes' post, since he has nothing new to react to. I'll post soon.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That is to say, once I'm fully awake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-16-2015, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T11:08:35-08:00","id":407956,"title":"","content":"Guy rolled 3 Successes to notice you guys noticing him...noticing you...noticing him...noticing...........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T16:43:56-08:00","id":408319,"title":"","content":"No ranks in Intimidation, and I don't think this fits in the prerogative of Persuasion, so....lets just see what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T03:09:56-08:00","id":408730,"title":"","content":"Well, Phoenix has got some Intimidation, so...<br /> <br /> [Intimidating the asshole: Presence + Intimidation = 5 dice; 1 success]<br /> <br /> Huh...kinda hoping for more, but hey, 5 dice, what can ya do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T03:41:38-08:00","id":408736,"title":"","content":"Do I get to post now or should I wait for you Techpriest to post the reaction of the bullies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T08:45:40-08:00","id":409016,"title":"","content":"You can always feel free to post in your turn order. Consider this the general rule: If I haven't responded to something yet, you can post or wait. If you choose to wait, you can simply post &quot;Waiting&quot; here in the OOC forum, just to make doubly sure that I know you're waiting for me to respond to something.<br /> <br /> In short, I'll never have a problem with you posting in your normal turn order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T09:18:12-08:00","id":409039,"title":"","content":"<b>Resist Intimidation</b>: Resolve + Composure - 4 Successes.<br /> <br /> The Initiative order is as follows:<br /> <br /> Bardo 15<br /> NPCs 11<br /> Astoria 9<br /> Crapcarp 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T14:23:24-08:00","id":409327,"title":"","content":"Ok, I want to Alter Conductivity on the shoes of that asshole and the part of the floor that goes from below his feet to the nearest wall socket. Luckily that would shock the bastard. You think that's posible?<br /> <br /> EDIT: in case it is:<br /> <br /> <b>Improvised Alter Conductivity:</b> Gnosis (2) + Matter (2) + Willpower (3) = 1, 1, 5, 5, 7, <b>9</b>, <b>10</b> (Re-roll= <b>10</b>) (Re-roll= <b>9</b>) = <b>4 Sucesses (8 Targets)</b> That should cover a rather big portion of the ground and the feet of the three assailtants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-17-2015, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T15:11:54-08:00","id":409359,"title":"","content":"Bardo, coming out swinging! They each take 4 Bashing Damage.<br /> <br /> If you're targeting the floor and relying on the conductivity of your own shoes to protect everyone else, then this should work. If you were trying to effect only part of the floor I think I would throw a -2 on there for precision. Given that this is effecting only the three men who just happen to be starting a fight, repeated uses of this might push it into Improbable Magic. So using it again here might require a Paradox Roll. Not that you'll have to, since it has a Prolonged duration. So bear in mind this will last for like an hour unless you cut it off early.<br /> <br /> I'll wait for you to post the narrative, then post their response. (Spoiler: Their response is to get deep fried)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T15:20:30-08:00","id":409363,"title":"","content":"Yeah, is probably a one-shot thing meaning he will dissipate it after the initial shock. Bardo doesn't want to badly harm anyone, he is a MD and takes the Hypocratic Oath seriously.<br /> <br /> EDIT: well, unless you guys prefer for the floor to keep frying them, that's it. Next turn they will had had 8 Bashing unless the get out the spot, wich should make them fall unconscious.<br /> <br /> I edited the IC post to remove the line where he dissipates the spell, we can always do it next turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-17-2015, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T16:58:37-08:00","id":409416,"title":"","content":"Head Asshole- Overcome Muscle Spasms: Strength + Willpower= 3 Successes<br /> 2nd Guy: - Overcome Muscle Spasms: Strength + Willpower = 6 Successes (I rolled three 10s in a row).<br /> <br /> Head Asshole's Attack: (Strength + Weaponry - Astoria's Defense + Mage Armor 5) = 0 Successes<br /> 2nd Guys Attack: (Strength + Weaponry - Bardo's Defense + Mage Armor 4) = 2 Successes.<br /> <br /> Bardo takes 2 Bashing Damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T20:32:55-08:00","id":409548,"title":"","content":"Regarding vulgar/covert magic, it's always been my interpretation that most spells can be either covert or vulgar depending on how it's being cast. Take Bardo's use of Alter Conductivity for example, I would think it would be vulgar considering that it results in three people getting electrocuted by impossible means. I know the spell description states that it's covert, but if you look at the rote description, it's used to cut off power to a building, and the spell certainly would be covert for that particular use.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, that's only my interpretation of it, doesn't have to be yours. I just thought I'd throw in my two cents on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T21:09:40-08:00","id":409624,"title":"","content":"You know, after reading over Improbable Magic and Hiding Magic in Plain Sight (Probable Magic), I agree. The example of using Destroy Object, a covert spell, to rot away a perfectly good platform being pushed into Improbability suggests that an Alter Conductivity spell used in this way would do the same.<br /> <br /> Thorbes: I have no intention of making you reroll after getting 4 Successes. You only have 1 Paradox die anyway. Go ahead and roll it. You could Mitigate with a point of Mana for a chance die or not as you like. If you do get a success, you could take it as Backlash.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, depending on where you keep your Matter tools, you could make use of them to reduce it to a chance die without the Mitigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-18-2015, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T23:16:44-08:00","id":409737,"title":"","content":"I have a question before I actually post.<br /> <br /> I'm not so much engaging as taking the briefcase on my turn. I know the other men were essentially swiping for it, but for me, it's in arm's reach? Do I have to roll to get it, or is it just assumed I'm not being held back/kept from it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T02:39:23-08:00","id":409835,"title":"","content":"I agree, is as Improbable as it gets. The Matter tools (and the Death tools too) are in pouches inside the coat. Yeah, they are at hand, but being honest, Bardo didn't thought of using them. It's his first Improbable spell, so he's going to learn not to forget about them the hard way. Also, ouch, my shoulder!<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox (1): </b>1 = <b>0 Successes</b><br /> <br /> Note it wasn't mitigated by either tools or Mana, so is a regular failure, not a Dramatic one.<br /> <br /> I also forgot to actualize my Willpower:<br /> <br /> <b>Current Willpower:</b> 4<br /> <br /> <b>Current Mana:</b> 4<br /> <br /> <b>Current Health:</b> 2 Bashing out of 7<br /> <br /> EDIT: as it is Improbable, remember that the sleepers present may Unravel it with Disbelief, so it very well may end after this first turn despite Bardo's intention of letting it keep running.<br /> There are like 7 sleepers present, right? The three thugs, the bartender and the waitress and I think another couple? Even if they have average Resolve+Composure (4) that would be around 28 dice for unraveling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. You can roll it, but I think is safe to asume it goes *puf* after the first turn <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-18-2015, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T06:34:02-08:00","id":410035,"title":"","content":"<b>Astoria:</b> Normally I would say you wouldn't have to roll, but since he is on the table actively trying to keep you from the briefcase by attacking, I think I'll require a Wits + Dexterity roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Thorbes:</b> You reminded me, the presence of the Sleepers adds a +2 to the Paradox Roll! You can roll the 2 extra dice separately, and just as before can retroactively have spent Mana and take Backlash as you choose.<br /> <br /> There are four Sleepers present. Hannah and the couple left, leaving Andrei and the attackers.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unraveling - Resolve + Composure</u><br /> Andrei: </b>2 Successes<br /> <b>Head Asshole: </b>1 Success<br /> <b>2nd Guy:</b> 2 Successes<br /> <b>3rd Guy: </b>0 Successes<br /> <br /> <b>*Poof*</b><br /> <br /> Oh, and by the way, for anyone planning on attacking or using other spells against the attackers, here are their relevant stats:<br /> <br /> <u>Head Asshole</u><br /> Defense: 3<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> Composure: 3<br /> <br /> <u>2nd Guy</u><br /> Defense: 2<br /> Resolve: 2<br /> Composure: 2<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-18-2015, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T07:17:55-08:00","id":410066,"title":"","content":"The Paradox is rolled either on a Vulgar or Improbable spell, but the +2 for witnesses says &quot;vulgar magic only&quot;. Anyway, just in case:<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox (2) : 9,10 </b>(Re-roll = <b>9</b>)<b> = 3 Successes!!! </b><br /> <br /> uh-oh....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, that would have taken 3 dice from my initial spell roll, lets say we take 1 success away instead? That's the average of 3 dice, though as this Paradox roll demonstrates that's hardly indication of anything...<br /> <br /> I'd better contain it as Backlash, unless you guys think it would be cool to have an Stygian Anomaly in the bar for the remaining hour/scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T07:53:10-08:00","id":410088,"title":"","content":"Also, does that weird abyssal-paiting-thing react in any way to the Paradox?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T08:26:29-08:00","id":410103,"title":"","content":"<i>Time 1 - Perfect Timing = Gnosis 1 + Time 1 + High Speech 2 = <b>8</b>, 6, 2, 4 = 1 die added to next roll (1 mana spent)</i><br /> <br /> <i>Grabbing that briefcase = Wits 3 + Dex 3 + Perfect Timing 1 = 1, 5, 6, 1, 5, 2, 5</i><br /> <br /> So that didn't go well...,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4859,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","user":"NoiseConspiracy","date":".  Adding mana cost 02-18-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T08:42:01-08:00","id":410128,"title":"","content":"<b>Thorbes: </b>You're absolutely right, you didn't have to roll that Paradox in the first place. Sorry about that. So we'll ignore that. (Which is good timing, considering that many successes on the Paradox roll).<br /> <br /> EDIT: You didn't have to roll those two dice I mean.<br /> <br /> <b>Astoria: </b>Since I would consider grabbing the briefcase to be a reflexive action, you can chant and grab in the same turn. Remember that now you're using High Speech directly in front of the Sleepers. The spells using High Speech before I allowed for whispering it in the corner of the bar, but in this case they should all be able to hear you. In the particular case of this spell, I don't think it would be pushed into improbability, so as far as they're concerned, you're just a weirdo. Also, don't forget Perfect Timing costs a point of Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-18-2015, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T08:55:18-08:00","id":410137,"title":"","content":"Yeah, she does come off a bit strange using it, I agree. And I will mark the Mana point accordingly on the previous post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:27:36-08:00","id":410202,"title":"","content":"We'll move straight on to Carp's post now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T10:41:34-08:00","id":410306,"title":"","content":"Phoenix wants one of the batons, so first he'll grapple the 2nd guy for this turn, and next turn he'll try to swipe it.<br /> <br /> [Grappling 2nd Guy: Strength + Brawl - Defense = 6 dice; 1 success]<br /> <br /> Huh, good thing grappling ain't contested, that might've been a problem otherwise. Though these guys seem to be getting lucky, so let's just hope his Strength of 4 will be enough penalty for the 2nd guy. Speaking of Strength, I'll have to know the 2nd guy's rating because that'll be a penalty for trying to take his weapon next turn (assuming the grapple is maintained, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:14:32-08:00","id":410349,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Stats</u></b><br /> Head Guy: Strength is 2, all other Attributes are 3.<br /> 2nd Guy: All Attributes are 2.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:45:27-08:00","id":410385,"title":"","content":"<b>Thorbes:</b> I edited my post to include a reaction by the entity in the painting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:03:43-08:00","id":410397,"title":"","content":"So, to be clear, Phoenix had grappled the guy that bludgeoned Bardo, right? Hmmm, we have that covered, the third guy will come up now that he is not being electrocuted, and the Head guy is still trying to grab the briefcase I supose.<br /> <br /> Ok, do you think I may be able to inject one of the anesthetics Bardo has in his doctor's bag to the second guy, now being grappled? Oh, that gives me another idea! Would you think I can use a Veiling of Matter to exchange the appearances of Bardo's doctor's bag and the briefcase? Let them go home with a bag full of medical implements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:57:09-08:00","id":410516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=410397#post410397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to be clear, Phoenix had grappled the guy that bludgeoned Bardo, right? Hmmm, we have that covered, the third guy will come up now that he is not being electrocuted, and the Head guy is still trying to grab the briefcase I supose.<br /> <br /> Ok, do you think I may be able to inject one of the anesthetics Bardo has in his doctor's bag to the second guy, now being grappled? Oh, that gives me another idea! Would you think I can use a Veiling of Matter to exchange the appearances of Bardo's doctor's bag and the briefcase? Let them go home with a bag full of medical implements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that'd be a good idea, considering that the Head guy is already going after the briefcase anyways and he would see the magic go off, too (not to mention an Abyssal's around). Injecting the anesthetics on the grappled guy would prevent any chance of him breaking free and might allow Phoenix to take the weapon <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">and wield it for an immediate attack (if it\u2019s allowed of course).</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:58:16-08:00","id":410557,"title":"","content":"<b>Thorbes: </b>Like Carp said, the Head Guy is basically right on top of the briefcase, since they're both on the table. He would see the exchange. So you would have to find some way of getting it out of their sight first (in such a way that wouldn't make them suspicious and check the case anyway). Getting syringe out from your back and preparing would definitely qualify as an instant action. So you'd have to wait next turn to inject it. However, as long as he doesn't break free, you wouldn't have to roll to administer it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You know, now that I think about it, if you guys are cool with waiving some of these mechanical restrictions for the sake of Play By Post flow, I'm good with that. I'm assuming you probably are, so Thorbes you can go ahead and use the syringe in this turn. If anyone has any objections, you can always edit it. I have to remind myself that Play By Posts work on a few different rules from in person games.<br /> <br /> It is also clear that the 3rd Guy isn't getting up any time soon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-18-2015, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:36:07-08:00","id":410650,"title":"","content":"I see, wish I had thought about it before.<br /> <br /> Ah, good to know about the third guy, that makes things easier.<br /> <br /> Ok, so if anyone is cool with it, I will give 2nd guy a shot of anesthetic. That'd leave only Indian guy to deal with and I supose some more anesthetic in the shape of a Phoenix-powered baton to the head should do the trick <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: so, no roll at all to administer it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:56:24-08:00","id":410664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=410650#post410650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: so, no roll at all to administer it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, Phoenix has got him pretty well pinned.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Head Guy </u><br /> Grabs the Briefcase: </b>Wits 3 + Dexterity 3 = 1 Success<br /> <b>Hauls Ass: </b>Stamina 3 + Athletics 2 = 1 Success<br /> <br /> So anyone chasing him down only has to get 1 Success to catch up with him right away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-18-2015, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T05:22:33-08:00","id":411327,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Catching the Bad Guy = Str 2 + Athletics 1 = 10, 6, 5 (exploding 10 produced 2) = 1 success </i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Grabbing the briefcase again = Dex 3 + Wits 3 = 10, 9, 9, 7, 3, 3 (exploding 10 produced 6) = 3 successes</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I recognize that, due to him being on the run, this may no longer be a Dex+Wits roll...I mostly made it for the sake of keeping things moving. In either case, if this doesn't take it from him, any chance it would put Astoria's hand on it enough to stop the bad guy?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T06:40:39-08:00","id":411422,"title":"","content":"This is fine for grabbing the briefcase, but he still has a hold of it himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:32:59-08:00","id":411745,"title":"","content":"You hear that, crapcarp? Need a little assistance over here...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:13:06-08:00","id":411982,"title":"","content":"Alright, so since the 2nd guy is unconscious, is it fair for Phoenix to grab the baton as a reflexive action then chase the Head guy and hit him, or will that take two turns? Also, I'm guessing that since Astoria's got a hold on the briefcase, Phoenix doesn't have to roll to chase the guy down, therefore it's just a matter of attacking him.<br /> <br /> [Attacking Head guy w/ Baton: Strength + Weaponry + Willpower + 3B Baton - 3 Defense = 10 dice \u2192 (7,3,(<b>10</b>,<b> 10</b>, 4),7,2,1,5,<b>8</b>,6,<b>9</b>,3) 4 successes]<br /> <br /> For this roll, I'm making two assumptions: 1.) Phoenix has the baton, if he needs a turn to take the baton, he'll forsake it in favor of chasing the Head guy and just fall back on his Muay Thai, so that's using Brawl instead along with the Specialty bonus of +1, so that means it's a total of 9 dice and I just take the last die away, resulting in 3 successes instead. 2.) The baton has a dice mod of 2B, if it's less, that's the same result with using Muay Thai (in terms of successes at least), but if it's more, I can always roll extra dice and edit this post accordingly.<br /> <br /> I've made a roll for chasing the Head guy just in case:<br /> <br /> [Chasing Head guy: Stamina + Athletics = 5 dice \u2192 (5,6,7,<b>9</b>,5) 1 success]<br /> <br /> By the way, I'm putting up Phoenix's current status on the same post that has his character sheet for easy reference. Just thought of doing that since I spent a Willpower actually.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Alright, I rolled another die and just got a 3, so that's still 4 successes anyways. But hey! Phoenix has a free 3B baton now, so that's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 02-19-2015, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:32:01-08:00","id":412001,"title":"","content":"Don't you have to substract the Head Guy's Defense (3)? That still left you with 4 Successes, enough to incapacitate him (he has 8 Health and that would put him in 8 Bashing! He will colapse sooner or later).<br /> <br /> EDIT: great idea about the Status, I also edited mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-19-2015, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:46:33-08:00","id":412032,"title":"","content":"I agree about status. I'll update mine when I'm on my computer and not a phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T14:18:05-08:00","id":412071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=412001#post412001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you have to substract the Head Guy's Defense (3)? That still left you with 4 Successes, enough to incapacitate him (he has 8 Health and that would put him in 8 Bashing! He will colapse sooner or later).<br /> <br /> EDIT: great idea about the Status, I also edited mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are absolutely right about that, I almost forgot, but it's cool, I changed it. Also, thanks for the compliment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T14:43:12-08:00","id":412093,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Crapcarp: </b>You can grab the baton no problem. Huh, I thought it was 2B too, but I just double checked it and it's 3. No need for the chasing roll. Nice work on the status thing. Very convenient for me.<br /> <br /> That takes him up to 8 Bashing Damage.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Head Guy</u></b><br /> <i>Stay Conscious: </i>Stamina + Willpower = 1 Success<br /> <br /> He has 4 Willpower Points left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-19-2015, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:08:09-08:00","id":412138,"title":"","content":"Ah, bollocks! He's still up. Wonder if a Ruling of Mind or Life would be enough to force the failure on the Stay Conscious roll? Also, Damage 3 Baton? I suddenly feel lucky I got away with only a bruised shoulder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:34:22-08:00","id":412158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=412138#post412138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, bollocks! He's still up. Wonder if a Ruling of Mind or Life would be enough to force the failure on the Stay Conscious roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using 'Trigger Autonomic Functions' from 'The Mysterium' pg. 196 as a base, I'd say a Life Ruling spell could push someone already near unconsciousness over the edge. He would get a contested resistance with his Stamina 3 (And what else is willpower fore but situations like this one), but he would have to beat whatever successes you get for the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:51:42-08:00","id":412167,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd give it a shot then. Just to be sure, that would be Covert, Covert, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't think I could dodge the Paradox bullet again.<br /> <br /> <b>Improvised Ruling Life Spell:</b> Gnosis (2) + Life (2) + Willpower (3) = 2, 3, 4, 5, <b>8</b>, <b>9</b>, <b>10</b> (Re-roll = <b>8</b>) = <b>4 Successes</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <br /> <b>Current Mana:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Current Willpower: </b>3<br /> <br /> Fingers crossed he gets less... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T16:48:09-08:00","id":412207,"title":"","content":"Haha. I was worried for a second there. I rolled: Stamina 3 + Willpower 3 = (1,2,<b>9</b>,6,<b>9</b>,<b>10</b>....and 4).<br /> <br /> You now have three unconscious dudes in a bar...now what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T17:10:13-08:00","id":412219,"title":"","content":"Well, that was close! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now we call the ambulance and take them to the Masachussets General Hospital, where I (and so, we) can have access to them. I plan on using transmuted distilled water turned into amobarbital, wich can act as a sort of &quot;truth serum&quot; so Astoria can interrogate them at her leisure and then I will clean any traces of the drug from both their system and my implements... it is kinda illegal to use it as part of interrogations and the testimony would be useless on a trial.<br /> <br /> I don't think we want the police to actually get into this, but the bartender already called them... any idea about how to deal with that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-19-2015, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:05:55-08:00","id":412366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=412207#post412207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You now have three unconscious dudes in a bar...now what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Our first order of business should be to see if they have some back-up waiting outside. Considering their determination, organization, and the fact that they at least had a rough idea of what they were dealing with, it's quite likely they do. The last thing we need is an ambush in a basement. On that note, Phoenix'll move the closest he can to the entrance without being spotted from the inside and try to detect any minds hanging outside.<br /> <br /> [Rote cast Sense Consciousness (M:tAw p. 206): Wits + Empathy + Mind + Willpower = 10 dice \u2192 (1,<b>9</b>,3,2,1,(<b>10</b>, 3),1,1,6,(<b>10</b>, <b>10</b>, 6)) 4 successes]<br /> <br /> Willpower: 3/5<br /> <br /> Alright, so that's an 8 yard radius to detect minds, and he'll focus on outside. At least they can't come in without him knowing about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=412219#post412219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now we call the ambulance and take them to the Masachussets General Hospital, where I (and so, we) can have access to them. I plan on using transmuted distilled water turned into amobarbital, wich can act as a sort of &quot;truth serum&quot; so Astoria can interrogate them at her leisure and then I will clean any traces of the drug from both their system and my implements... it is kinda illegal to use it as part of interrogations and the testimony would be useless on a trial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea on the ambulance, that way we'll know exactly where they are when we get the time to interrogate them.<br /> <br /> As for removing the truth serum, you don't have to remove it at all actually. Just let the spell wear off and it'll turn back into water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=412219#post412219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we want the police to actually get into this, but the bartender already called them... any idea about how to deal with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh fuck no, we don't! We need to leave before they get here. We should take Meristoktrix with us to a safer location to talk about this. I don't think it's a good idea to take him to the Nest, but we don't have a whole lot of options either...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 02-19-2015, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T21:13:57-08:00","id":412410,"title":"","content":"Well, the first order of business is confirming that Meristoktrix is still there, and didn't run off in the encounter. I doubt he would, but you never know.<br /> <br /> Second, the bartender said he <i>would</i> call the cops, but technically the encounter was over within a second or two of that. If it hasn't happened yet, I'd love a chance to speak up.<br /> <br /> Third, we will take Meristoktrix with us back to the Nest (<i>unless I'm outnumbered on that decision, at which I'll concede</i>). They're not after him as much as they're after the scroll, which will already be in the Nest with me, so he doesn't present that much more risk to the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T02:25:29-08:00","id":412577,"title":"","content":"Ok, I would also, for the sake of verosimilitude decay the shoe soles and the electrical outlet on the wall. I should also make sure the feet of the three thugs are wet with snow. That would mostly cover the &quot;weird electrification&quot; we have sleeper witnesses of and give it a filmsy if logical explanation.<br /> <br /> Good thinking on the backup, crapcarp, we don't want to get jumped on with our guard down.<br /> <br /> And yeah, now that you mention it, NoiseConspiracy, Meristoktrix have been quite &quot;absent&quot; during the whole brouhaha. Is (was?) the guy around? Maybe he can help us cover up this mess. Also, hoping the bartender dindn't still call the cops. I can handle the hospital staff, but cops...<br /> <br /> OK, the Decay spell is Vulgar, so can I asumme you guys can keep our only sleeper witness from actually witnessing anything? That painting thing is creeping me out. I will use my Death tool to get the Paradox down to a chance die, but I will have to cast it 4 times and I don't trust my chances if I have to deal with that +2.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm cool with taking Meristoktrix to The Nest. As crapcarp said, we don't have a whole lot of options.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: I will post the resolution of the fight at least on the IC thread, when we finally decide what to do next maybe Techpriest or us can move things along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-20-2015, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T02:54:58-08:00","id":412584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, now that I think about it, if you guys are cool with waiving some of these mechanical restrictions for the sake of Play By Post flow, I'm good with that. I'm assuming you probably are, so Thorbes you can go ahead and use the syringe in this turn. If anyone has any objections, you can always edit it. I have to remind myself that Play By Posts work on a few different rules from in person games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking about this and I have a &quot;houserule&quot; to offer.<br /> <br /> So, normally you can in the same turn move up to your Speed and do an Instant Action. You can forgo your Instant Action to run, effectively moving twice your Speed in that turn.<br /> <br /> Ok, so how about we can do it backwards and if you don't move, you can change that for another Instant Action that cannot be used to attack or cast spells? It would be used for things that do take a turn like aiming, or preparing a weapon, those sort of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T05:08:12-08:00","id":412644,"title":"","content":"<b>Paradox </b>(1)<b>:</b> 7 <b>(0 Successes)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Decay Spell (1st guy shoes):</b> Gnosis (2) + Death (2) + High Speech (2) = 3,3,3,5,7,<b>10</b> (Re-roll=4) = <b>1 Success.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Paradox </b>(2)<b>:</b> 5, <b>9</b> <b>(1 Success)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Decay Spell (2nd guy shoes):</b> Gnosis (2) + Death (2) + High Speech (2) = 3,3,6,<b>8</b>,<b>9,9 </b>= <b>3 Successes.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Paradox </b>(3)<b>:</b> 1,1,<b>10</b> (Re-roll=2) <b>(1 Success)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Decay Spell (3rd guy shoes):</b> Gnosis (2) + Death (2) + High Speech (2) = 2,2,5,7,<b>9, 9</b> = <b>2 Successes.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Paradox </b>(4)<b>:</b> 1,3,6,7 <b>(0 Successes)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Decay Spell (electrical outlet):</b> Gnosis (2) + Death (2) + High Speech (2) = 1,2,3,4,7,<b>10</b> (Re-roll=<b>10</b>) (Re-roll=<b>10</b>) (Re-roll=7) = <b>3 Successes.</b><br /> <br /> EDIT: misread the +1 Paradox being per each previous Paradox, not Paradox <i>roll</i>. Is fixed now, I substracted 1 success per each Paradox penalty. Bardo absorbs those 2 Paradoxes as Backlash, I will mark them bolded in the Status. The 2 other Bashing he received will be both gone in a minute due to the Life spell, but those Backlash ones being Resistant I think should take the regular amount of time (15 min. each).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-20-2015, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T07:44:48-08:00","id":412765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=412584#post412584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been thinking about this and I have a &quot;houserule&quot; to offer.<br /> <br /> So, normally you can in the same turn move up to your Speed and do an Instant Action. You can forgo your Instant Action to run, effectively moving twice your Speed in that turn.<br /> <br /> Ok, so how about we can do it backwards and if you don't move, you can change that for another Instant Action that cannot be used to attack or cast spells? It would be used for things that do take a turn like aiming, or preparing a weapon, those sort of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer it not to allow things that offer a combat bonus, like aiming. That would have a surprising effect on the game's lethality. But for grabbing an object, or even drawing a weapon, I'm fine with this. But obviously, anything you can do, the baddies can do.<br /> <br /> Also, your spellcasting roll doesn't take a Paradox penalty when you absorb the Paradox with Backlash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T07:56:37-08:00","id":412797,"title":"","content":"Uh...<br /> <br /> Ok, I should add back the successes then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T22:08:36-08:00","id":413797,"title":"","content":"<i>Persuade Andrei to please not call the Police. Manipulation 3 + Persuade 1 = <b>9</b>, <b>8</b>, 4, 1 = 2 successes<br /> <br /> <br /> If Manipulation is the wrong attribute, both my Presence and Composure are also 3, so it's basically a wash if I was wrong.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T16:16:42-08:00","id":414570,"title":"","content":"I'll be posting soon.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In the meantime, what other RPGs and such are you guys into?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T06:31:35-08:00","id":415083,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.<br /> <br /> I grew up playing Classic WoD games...mostly Mage and Changeling, although I own at least one edition of all the core lines. Most of my friends are pretty hardcore about D&amp;D, so that's usually what I play with an actual tabletop group these days, but online it's mostly WoD games. <br /> <br /> I actually hated the nWoD at first, because I got really personal about it. &quot;How dare they restrict Magic in new Mage&quot; or &quot;how can you have Vampires without the Camarilla&quot; and all that. It wasn't until I played Geist four years ago or so that I started giving it a shot. Mechanically, I greatly prefer the nWoD at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:17:43-08:00","id":415595,"title":"","content":"If you guys like we can put this scene to rest and jump forward in time to whenever/wherever you'd like. The Nest, the Hospital, etc.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <b>Thorbes: </b>Waiting for the ambulance should give your resistant bashing time to heal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-22-2015, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:24:14-08:00","id":415599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NoiseConspiracy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=415083#post415083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough.<br /> <br /> I grew up playing Classic WoD games...mostly Mage and Changeling, although I own at least one edition of all the core lines. Most of my friends are pretty hardcore about D&amp;D, so that's usually what I play with an actual tabletop group these days, but online it's mostly WoD games.<br /> <br /> I actually hated the nWoD at first, because I got really personal about it. &quot;How dare they restrict Magic in new Mage&quot; or &quot;how can you have Vampires without the Camarilla&quot; and all that. It wasn't until I played Geist four years ago or so that I started giving it a shot. Mechanically, I greatly prefer the nWoD at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started out with old school D&amp;D, back when Elf and Dwarf were a class<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With World of Darkness I actually started with Werewolf the Forsaken, which gives me something of a skewed perspective compared to many &quot;Classic WoD is better than anything EVAR&quot; folks. Werewolf the Forsaken is one of my favorite all time games, with Mage a close second. The only Old WoD game I'm familiar with is Vampire: The Masquerade, and Requiem pales in comparison (But is still perfectly solid, and certainly enjoyable). I also really like the Warhammer 40k games, as its my favorite Sci Fi Universe.<br /> <br /> There a variety of games I've been looking at lately for a change of pace. Mutants and Masterminds, FATE, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:05:25-08:00","id":415739,"title":"","content":"Started with AD&amp;D and Lord of the Rings in high school. Later I got into Wod through Vampire the Masquerade and later Requiem when I actually became an active part of the comunity. First in spanish forums and then here. I got into almost all of the nWoD games but Mage and Vampire will always be my favourite. Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd edition is looking quite sexy too. Changelling is a work of art.<br /> <br /> I play a lot of different rpgs: Warhammer Fantasy (1st and 2nd edition), Edge of the Empire (Star Wars), Aquelarre (spanish roleplaying game, apparently quite famous beyond our borders too), A Song of Ice and Fire, Legend of the 5 Rings (2nd-3rd and 4th editions), D&amp;D (3th, 4th edtions and some retroclones), Yggdrasill, Call/Trail of Cthulu and now I'm trying to get into Ars Magica (5th ed.). That plus a lot of indie minigames of the most varied themes and settings. <hr /><br /> Back into story stuff: I'm ok with whatever you guys want to do. We could go to the hospital and do the interrogation or keep that as background* (or sort of flashback) and go back to the Nest.<br /> <br /> *Meaning, doing any relevant rolls here and gloss over it in the IC thread. Though Bardo should be going back home soon, he wakes up in 3 hours! (fortunately the Life spell will let him function with only that no problem).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:19:17-08:00","id":415951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=414570#post414570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the meantime, what other RPGs and such are you guys into?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've only recently begun delving into TTRPGs actually. Although, when I was little, my siblings use to play AD&amp;D <i>all the time</i>. I wanted to join in of course, but they wouldn't let me due to the game's complexity (also, I didn't have the right mentality to play it back then anyways). So for more than a decade I've had a hunger for playing TTRPGs, but never really found an outlet for it.<br /> <br /> That is, until I saw Cardians early last year, which is a group that organizes Hunter: the Vigil games on deviantART. Curious, I did a little research and I've been hooked on nWoD ever since (don't know much about cWoD though). I bought book after book, especially Mage books because I really love the potential of the game and there's so much material to it. My favorites thus far (besides Mage, of course) are Changeling and Hunter, though I have the corebooks of Vampire, Werewolf, and Geist as well.<br /> <br /> Besides WoD, I've also been playing some D&amp;D (finally), and I'm looking at designing one myself. 'Course, I wanna get some more experience before I get really serious on that project.<br /> <hr /><br /> Back to AoP: It is getting late, so we might have to pick another time to meet Meristo again or something (probably at the Nest or some other more secure and secluded location). I think a timeskip would be best at this point, as I don't really see anything else we need to do in this scene. We could also move on to interrogating the three guys or the second meeting with Meristo in any order, whichever would work better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:01:56-08:00","id":416198,"title":"","content":"Well, Astoria's priority is to get to cracking on this scroll, so I'm okay with a Time Skip. I'm okay mostly surmising what we found through interrogation through flashback/single post things, if that's what you're implying, and get to the bigger meetings...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T03:40:12-08:00","id":416337,"title":"","content":"Yep, the interrogation may be a couple or so rolls by all of us:<br /> <br /> Bardo: getting access to the patients and Trasmute Water into &quot;truth serum&quot; (this acts as a +3 Equipment Bonus* for your interrogation rolls)<br /> <br /> Astoria: &quot;Good cop&quot; interrogation (using Persuassion)<br /> <br /> Phoenix: &quot;Bad cop&quot; interrogation (using Intimidate)<br /> <br /> *I don't know if their situation would also count as another Equipment bonus, after al they are completely at our mercy. We can literally off them at any point without anyone being none the wiser.<br /> <br /> By the way, Techpriest, appart form the radios did they have any kind of ID, say a driver's license or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:57:26-08:00","id":416498,"title":"","content":"You could also split up. Astoria could work on the scroll while Bardo and Phoenix interrogate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:37:25-08:00","id":416764,"title":"","content":"This is true. Astoria would interrogate if it was pressing, but this scroll has her focus unless it is actually required elsewhere...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:17:27-08:00","id":416814,"title":"","content":"That's another way, yeah. Spliting up is not that troublesome in this medium, is it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:40:18-08:00","id":416898,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah <b>Thorbes</b>. You did find ID on them. According to their driver's licensees, their names are Talat Reddy (Indian guy), Mark Hogan (Bald guy), and Warren Fox (Young guy). Each license is from a different State: Colorado, Illanois, and Wisconsin respectively. Each wallet also has a credit card, but little else.<br /> <br /> So I'll establish two separate scenes for us: Bardo and Phoenix in the Hospital - Astoria and Meristo at the Nest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:50:52-08:00","id":416908,"title":"","content":"Works for me, but let's wait for crapcarp to comfirm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:53:51-08:00","id":416940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=416898#post416898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah <b>Thorbes</b>. You did find ID on them. According to their driver's licensees, their names are Talat Reddy (Indian guy), Mark Hogan (Bald guy), and Warren Fox (Young guy). Each license is from a different State: Colorado, Illanois, and Wisconsin respectively. Each wallet also has a credit card, but little else.<br /> <br /> So I'll establish two separate scenes for us: Bardo and Phoenix in the Hospital - Astoria and Meristo at the Nest?</div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me. I presume Bardo will relay their names to Phoenix for the purposes of interrogation. 'Course, they're probably fake licenses, but it's something at least. And hey, Phoenix can use Mind and Bardo can use Life to see whether they're lying or not when answering the questions. By the way, are our characters considered to have a day of rest to regain a point of Willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T16:09:12-08:00","id":416951,"title":"","content":"Alright. So I'll set the new scenes for us, after a night of rest. And yes, everyone gets a point of <b>Willpower </b>back. I'll establish the time of the interrogation to be around noon or so. Whenever we skip ahead in time you can always feel free to describe what your characters did in the interim.<br /> <br /> <b>Thorbes: </b>I've also rethought the aiming as a part of an extra instant action, and I'm fine with it. By the way, you can feel free to add life to Bardo's wife, effectively controlling the character. Same goes for any background characters you guys might want for <b>Astoria </b>or <b>Phoenix</b>. Obviously these can only be background characters, and not anyone that adds a mechanical advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T03:21:57-08:00","id":417399,"title":"","content":"Are you ok with Bardo taking the 1 Mana from the Hallow? He's quite drained, though none of you are full either. I could also scourge a dot of Stamina for +3 Mana though that would seriously weaken him (Stamina 1... low Health and Spell Tolerance). He is used to be that weak though.<br /> <br /> @crapcarp: of course he shares that information with Phoenix. I also though they might be false, but I have no idea how to check that. None of us have the skills or contacts to do so, or have we? What would be the roll? Wits + Larceny?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T05:48:13-08:00","id":417457,"title":"","content":"You can take the Mana point, far as I'm concerned. You've done more to earn it at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:55:43-08:00","id":418010,"title":"","content":"Sorry it took so long to write something so short. I spent most of the time trying to think of what else I could add. Bit of a case of writers block.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Although now that I look at the times, I guess it wasn't really that long. Just felt longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T16:12:03-08:00","id":418062,"title":"","content":"I think we might have to change the post order to keep things a little more organized. I suppose we could re-roll initiative (it <i>is</i> a new scene after all), but the main thing is to keep the two groups separate in the order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T17:41:11-08:00","id":418136,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Astoria: </b>Decoding the scroll will be an extended action of Intelligence + Investigation with your Cryptography specialty. Go ahead and make five rolls, with each roll representing an hour of work. (Five rolls because that's your dice pool, as per the limits on extended actions).<br /> <br /> You guys can do handle the post order here however you want. I originally intended to only require an Initiative roll per chapter, but this is my first Play by Post, and I didn't fully appreciate the difference in pacing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T21:17:33-08:00","id":418364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=418062#post418062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we might have to change the post order to keep things a little more organized. I suppose we could re-roll initiative (it <i>is</i> a new scene after all), but the main thing is to keep the two groups separate in the order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's flip places, cc. You and Thorbes post, and I'll go after you. That way we're not proverbially crossing the streams or anything like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T00:52:20-08:00","id":418493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NoiseConspiracy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=418364#post418364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's flip places, cc. You and Thorbes post, and I'll go after you. That way we're not proverbially crossing the streams or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that works.<br /> <br /> By the way Techpriest, how are you gonna handle XP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T02:13:29-08:00","id":418520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way Techpriest, how are you gonna handle XP? </div> </div> </div>Good question, I already know what I want to focus on.<br /> <br /> By the way, in adition to Scourge a dot of Stamina and (hopefully, if rolls don't fail me) perform an Oblation, I want Bardo to Dedicate one of his scalpels as a (weapon) Path Tool (Tome of Mysteries p. 106).<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicating Scalpel: </b><br /> Gnosis (2) + Composure (4) = 5,6,7,<b>8</b>,<b>9</b>,<b>10</b> (Re-roll=2) = <b>3</b>/5 <b>Successes</b> (10 min.)<br /> Gnosis (2) + Composure (4) = 2,5,5,<b>9</b>,<b>9</b>,<b>9</b> = <b>6</b>/5 <b>Successes</b> (<b>20 min. total</b>)<br /> <br /> <b>Oblation: </b>Gnosis (2) + Composure (4) = 1,4,<b>8</b>,<b>8</b>,<b>10</b>,<b>10</b> (Re-roll= 1,<b>8</b>) = <b>5 Successes</b> (1 Hour. <b>+1 Mana</b>)<br /> <br /> <b>Scourge Pattern:</b> <b>+3 Mana</b>. -1 Stamina (-1 Health. -1 Spell Tolerance) for 24 hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:55:42-08:00","id":418730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power?p=418493#post418493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way Techpriest, how are you gonna handle XP?</div> </div> </div> </div>I originally structured it to hand out XP at the end of each Chapter. Again, I'll have to make adjustments for the pacing. I'll have to think about this and get back to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:40:44-08:00","i